 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Explore taxonomy RDF — local SPARQL queries\n",
    "\n",
    "Uses `rdflib` to load the generated TTL bundles locally and run SPARQL queries interactively.  \n",
    "No server required — edit queries in-place and re-run cells.\n",
    "\n",
    "Once a query looks good, copy it to **[SPARQLQueries](https://github.com/pathway-lod/SPARQLQueries)** and add it to **[Snorql-UI](https://github.com/pathway-lod/Snorql-UI)**.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Kernel:** select `plantmetwiki-rdf` (register once with `python -m ipykernel install --user --name plantmetwiki-rdf`).\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## ⚠️ Limitations — read before writing queries\n",
    "\n",
    "`rdflib` is a pure-Python in-memory SPARQL engine with **no query optimizer**. Keep queries simple:\n",
    "\n",
    "| ✅ Works well | ❌ Avoid |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Simple `SELECT` with 1–2 triple patterns | Cartesian products (`?a` × `?b` with no shared variable) |\n",
    "| `COUNT` / `GROUP BY` on one variable | `FILTER(STRSTARTS(?a, STR(?b)))` over large sets — O(n²), very slow |\n",
    "| Queries on the small taxonomy bundle (~4 MB) | Loading the 300 MB core bundle (minutes + several GB RAM) |\n",
    "| Single-bundle queries | Cross-bundle joins (taxonomy + core together) |\n",
    "\n",
    "**URI structure note:** pathway URIs and DataNode URIs do **not** share a common string prefix:\n",
    "```\n",
    "Pathway:  http://rdf-plantmetwiki.bioinformatics.nl/pathways/PC1_r<version>\n",
    "DataNode: http://rdf-plantmetwiki.bioinformatics.nl/Pathway/PC1_r<version>/DataNode/<id>\n",
    "```\n",
    "(`pathways/` vs `Pathway/` — different case and path). `STRSTARTS(?node, STR(?pathway))` will never match.\n",
    "\n",
    "**For cross-layer queries** (e.g. "which pathway contains which species"), use the **Virtuoso** production endpoint where `wp:isPartOf` links DataNodes to their pathway across both graphs."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from rdflib import Graph, Namespace\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "WP   = Namespace(\"http://vocabularies.wikipathways.org/wp#\")\n",
    "NCBI = Namespace(\"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_\")\n",
    "\n",
    "PREFIXES = \"\"\"\n",
    "PREFIX wp:   <http://vocabularies.wikipathways.org/wp#>\n",
    "PREFIX ncbi: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_>\n",
    "PREFIX pmw:  <http://rdf-plantmetwiki.bioinformatics.nl/>\n",
    "PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "def sparql(g: Graph, query: str) -> pd.DataFrame:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Run a SPARQL SELECT and return a DataFrame.\"\"\"\n",
    "    results = g.query(PREFIXES + query)\n",
    "    return pd.DataFrame(results, columns=[str(v) for v in results.vars])\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Ready.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Load the taxonomy extra bundle\n",
    "\n",
    "This is the **taxonomy-only** bundle (~4 MB) — loads in a few seconds.\n",
    "\n",
    "It contains exclusively `wp:organism` triples — nothing else:\n",
    "- `?pathway wp:organism ncbi:33090` — one triple per pathway/reaction (Viridiplantae)\n",
    "- `?dataNode wp:organism ncbi:<taxon>` — one triple per annotated gene/protein/metabolite DataNode\n",
    "- `?biologicalEntityURI wp:organism ncbi:<taxon>` — same species repeated on the UniProt/TAIR/etc. URI\n",
    "\n",
    "The total triple count (~27K) is **much smaller** than the full PlantMetWiki graph (~3.8M triples),\n",
    "which also includes all WikiPathways RDF (DataNode labels, types, Xrefs, interactions, citations, etc.)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "VERSION = \"plantcyc17.0.0-gpml2021\"\n",
    "taxonomy_file = Path(f\"../output/bundles/all_gpml_taxonomy_extra-{VERSION}.ttl\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Loading {taxonomy_file} ...\")\n",
    "g = Graph()\n",
    "g.parse(str(taxonomy_file), format=\"turtle\")\n",
    "print(f\"Loaded {len(g):,} triples  ← all of these are wp:organism statements\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 1. Pathway-level: Viridiplantae coverage\n",
    "\n",
    "Every pathway and reaction should carry `wp:organism ncbi:33090` (Viridiplantae, NCBI:33090).\n",
    "\n",
    "Note: this query counts **unique subjects** (pathway/reaction URIs), not the total number of triples."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# How many distinct pathway/reaction URIs have wp:organism ncbi:33090?\n",
    "# Expected: 2478 (1162 pathways + 1316 reactions)\n",
    "sparql(g, \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT (COUNT(DISTINCT ?resource) AS ?resources_with_viridiplantae)\n",
    "WHERE {\n",
    "    ?resource wp:organism ncbi:33090 .\n",
    "}\n",
    "\"\"\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Sample pathway URIs — confirm they have the /pathways/ URI pattern\n",
    "sparql(g, \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT ?pathway\n",
    "WHERE {\n",
    "    ?pathway wp:organism ncbi:33090 .\n",
    "    FILTER(CONTAINS(STR(?pathway), \"/pathways/\"))\n",
    "}\n",
    "LIMIT 10\n",
    "\"\"\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 2. DataNode-level: per-species annotations\n",
    "\n",
    "Genes, proteins and metabolites with a `SPECIES` field in PlantCyc carry individual `wp:organism` triples.\n",
    "\n",
    "Note: each annotated DataNode contributes **two triples** — one on the GPML DataNode URI and one on the biological entity URI (UniProt, TAIR, etc.). The counts below reflect unique URIs."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# How many distinct URIs have a species annotation other than Viridiplantae?\n",
    "# Includes both DataNode URIs and biological entity URIs (UniProt, TAIR, ...)\n",
    "sparql(g, \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT (COUNT(DISTINCT ?node) AS ?annotated_uris)\n",
    "WHERE {\n",
    "    ?node wp:organism ?species .\n",
    "    FILTER(?species != ncbi:33090)\n",
    "}\n",
    "\"\"\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Only count DataNode URIs (exclude biological entity URIs)\n",
    "sparql(g, \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT (COUNT(DISTINCT ?node) AS ?annotated_datanode_uris)\n",
    "WHERE {\n",
    "    ?node wp:organism ?species .\n",
    "    FILTER(?species != ncbi:33090)\n",
    "    FILTER(CONTAINS(STR(?node), \"/DataNode/\"))\n",
    "}\n",
    "\"\"\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Species distribution across DataNode URIs — top 20\n",
    "sparql(g, \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT ?species (COUNT(DISTINCT ?node) AS ?node_count)\n",
    "WHERE {\n",
    "    ?node wp:organism ?species .\n",
    "    FILTER(?species != ncbi:33090)\n",
    "    FILTER(CONTAINS(STR(?node), \"/DataNode/\"))\n",
    "}\n",
    "GROUP BY ?species\n",
    "ORDER BY DESC(?node_count)\n",
    "LIMIT 20\n",
    "\"\"\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Sample DataNode URIs annotated with Arabidopsis thaliana (ncbi:3702)\n",
    "sparql(g, \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT ?node\n",
    "WHERE {\n",
    "    ?node wp:organism ncbi:3702 .\n",
    "    FILTER(CONTAINS(STR(?node), \"/DataNode/\"))\n",
    "}\n",
    "LIMIT 10\n",
    "\"\"\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 3. Biological entity URIs with species\n",
    "\n",
    "The taxonomy script annotates both the GPML DataNode URI **and** the biological identifier URI (UniProt, TAIR, etc.) with `wp:organism`, so downstream tools linking on those identifiers also pick up the species."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# UniProt URIs with their species annotation\n",
    "sparql(g, \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT ?entity ?species\n",
    "WHERE {\n",
    "    ?entity wp:organism ?species .\n",
    "    FILTER(STRSTARTS(STR(?entity), \"https://identifiers.org/uniprot/\"))\n",
    "}\n",
    "LIMIT 10\n",
    "\"\"\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# TAIR gene name URIs with their species annotation\n",
    "sparql(g, \"\"\"\n",
    "SELECT ?entity ?species\n",
    "WHERE {\n",
    "    ?entity wp:organism ?species .\n",
    "    FILTER(STRSTARTS(STR(?entity), \"https://identifiers.org/tair.name/\"))\n",
    "}\n",
    "LIMIT 10\n",
    "\"\"\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 4. Cross-layer queries → use Virtuoso\n",
    "\n",
    "Queries that join the taxonomy graph with the core WikiPathways graph (e.g. "which pathway contains which species?") require `wp:isPartOf` which lives in the core bundle — not this file.\n",
    "\n",
    "Run these on the **Virtuoso production endpoint** using named graphs:\n",
    "\n",
    "```sparql\n",
    "# Pathways containing at least one Arabidopsis thaliana node\n",
    "PREFIX wp:   <http://vocabularies.wikipathways.org/wp#>\n",
    "PREFIX ncbi: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_>\n",
    "\n",
    "SELECT ?pathway (COUNT(DISTINCT ?node) AS ?arabidopsis_nodes)\n",
    "WHERE {\n",
    "  GRAPH <http://rdf-plantmetwiki.bioinformatics.nl/graph/pathways> {\n",
    "      ?node wp:isPartOf ?pathway .\n",
    "  }\n",
    "  GRAPH <http://rdf-plantmetwiki.bioinformatics.nl/graph/gpml-taxonomy-extra> {\n",
    "      ?node wp:organism ncbi:3702 .\n",
    "  }\n",
    "}\n",
    "GROUP BY ?pathway\n",
    "ORDER BY DESC(?arabidopsis_nodes)\n",
    "LIMIT 20\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "```sparql\n",
    "# Multi-species pathways (nodes spanning more than one species)\n",
    "PREFIX wp:   <http://vocabularies.wikipathways.org/wp#>\n",
    "PREFIX ncbi: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_>\n",
    "\n",
    "SELECT ?pathway (COUNT(DISTINCT ?species) AS ?species_count)\n",
    "WHERE {\n",
    "  GRAPH <http://rdf-plantmetwiki.bioinformatics.nl/graph/pathways> {\n",
    "      ?node wp:isPartOf ?pathway .\n",
    "  }\n",
    "  GRAPH <http://rdf-plantmetwiki.bioinformatics.nl/graph/gpml-taxonomy-extra> {\n",
    "      ?node wp:organism ?species .\n",
    "      FILTER(?species != ncbi:33090)\n",
    "  }\n",
    "}\n",
    "GROUP BY ?pathway\n",
    "HAVING (?species_count > 1)\n",
    "ORDER BY DESC(?species_count)\n",
    "LIMIT 20\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 5. Sandbox — write your own queries here\n",
    "\n",
    "Edit and re-run. When a query is validated, copy it to **[SPARQLQueries](https://github.com/pathway-lod/SPARQLQueries)**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
